 </mrow></annotation-xml></semantics></math>
</div></section>
  <section data-depth="2" id="fs-id1165135176661"><h4 data-type="title">Identifying Special Angles Measured in Radians</h4>
   <p id="fs-id1165137924367">In addition to knowing the measurements in degrees and radians of a quarter revolution, a half  revolution, and a full revolution, there are other frequently encountered angles in one revolution of a circle with which we should be familiar. It is common to encounter multiples of 30, 45, 60, and 90 degrees. These values are shown in <a href="5-1-angles#Figure_05_01_016" class="autogenerated-content" aria-label="View Figure 14">Figure 14</a>. Memorizing these angles will be very useful as we study the properties associated with angles.</p>

   <div class="os-figure" id="Figure_05_01_016"><figure data-id="Figure_05_01_016" class="small ui-has-child-figcaption"><span data-type="media" id="fs-id1165133434666" data-alt="A graph of a circle with angles of 0, 30, 45, 60, 90, 120, 135, 150, 180, 210, 225, 240, 270, 300, 315, and 330 degrees.">
     <button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of A graph of a circle with angles of 0, 30, 45, 60, 90, 120, 135, 150, 180, 210, 225, 240, 270, 300, 315, and 330 degrees." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/a20fd561b53f935f89f6f0c484b6131dad90ab56" data-media-type="image/jpg" alt="A graph of a circle with angles of 0, 30, 45, 60, 90, 120, 135, 150, 180, 210, 225, 240, 270, 300, 315, and 330 degrees." width="487" height="406" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/a20fd561b53f935f89f6f0c484b6131dad90ab56"></button>
    </span>

   <figcaption class="os-caption-container">
  <span class="os-title-label">Figure </span>
<span class="os-number">14</span>



  <span class="os-divider"> </span>
  <span class="os-caption">Commonly encountered angles measured in degrees</span>
</figcaption></figure></div><p id="fs-id1165134297659">Now, we can list the corresponding radian values for the common measures of a circle corresponding to those listed in <a href="5-1-angles#Figure_05_01_016" class="autogenerated-content" aria-label="View Figure 14">Figure 14</a>, which are shown in <a href="5-1-angles#Figure_05_01_017" class="autogenerated-content" aria-label="View Figure 15">Figure 15</a>. Be sure you can verify each of these measures.</p>

   <div class="os-figure" id="Figure_05_01_017"><figure data-id="Figure_05_01_017" class="small ui-has-child-figcaption"><span data-type="media" id="fs-id1165135706783" data-alt="A graph of a circle with angles of 0, 30, 45, 60, 90, 120, 135, 150, 180, 210, 225, 240, 270, 300, 315, and 330 degrees. The graph also shows the equivalent amount of radians for each angle of degrees. For example, 30 degrees is equal to pi/6 radians.">
     <button type="button" aria-label="Click to enlarge image of A graph of a circle with angles of 0, 30, 45, 60, 90, 120, 135, 150, 180, 210, 225, 240, 270, 300, 315, and 330 degrees. The graph also shows the equivalent amount of radians for each angle of degrees. For example, 30 degrees is equal to pi/6 radians." class="image-button-wrapper"><img src="/apps/image-cdn/v1/f=webp/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/e1489bed5b8419f1f5fe96765087dbe49058cf43" data-media-type="image/jpg" alt="A graph of a circle with angles of 0, 30, 45, 60, 90, 120, 135, 150, 180, 210, 225, 240, 270, 300, 315, and 330 degrees. The graph also shows the equivalent amount of radians for each angle of degrees. For example, 30 degrees is equal to pi/6 radians." width="487" height="485" loading="lazy" data-original-src="/apps/archive/20260604.144757/resources/e1489bed5b8419f1f5fe96765087dbe49058cf43"></button>
    </span>

   <figcaption class="os-caption-container">
  <span class="os-title-label">Figure </span>
<span class="os-number">15</span>



  <span class="os-divider"> </span>
  <span class="os-caption">Commonly encountered angles measured in radians</span>
</figcaption></figure></div><div data-type="example" id="Example_05_01_02" class="ui-has-child-title"><header><h3 class="os-title">
  <span class="os-title-label">Example </span>
  <span class="os-number">2</span>
